=== 2. equipment precision fields, all 15 tactics ===

--- pilot-data.json (tactics[].equipment.{line_test_lb,lure_weight_oz,retrieve.pause_seconds}.precision)
+++ corrected
-"precision": "exact"
+"precision": "general"
(applies to all numeric equipment ranges across all 15 tactics -- none of the 15 tactics'
line-test, lure-weight, or pause-duration numbers are stated by any fetched DNR source;
they are self-authored "standard tackle" figures. Per instruction 2: "never manufacture a
range merely to fill the schema" -- general/estimated precision, not exact, is the honest
label. This does not remove the numbers; it stops the schema from implying a sourced
number where none exists.)

=== 3. regulation_provision: catch_and_release_permitted (statewide) ===

--- pilot-data.json (provisions[4].evidence / claim linkage)
+++ corrected
 The provision currently cites the Mille Lacs walleye-limit news release as its sole
 evidence. That release does not state a general catch-and-release permission.
-No correction applied automatically -- this requires either:
+  (a) a real MN DNR citation that actually states this rule, replacing the current
+      mis-cited claim, OR
+  (b) if no such citation is found, downgrading this provision's own status to
+      "needs_verification" (a new status value, not yet in the enum) rather than
+      leaving it implying DNR support it doesn't have.
 Flagged, not silently fixed, because fixing it requires new research, not a schema edit.

